## CodeQL full-scope comparison: main vs PR head (2026-10-30, local)
# Why: CI's PR-run CodeQL counts were far below main's (high 120, medium 8, no critical, vs main's
# critical 10, high 164, medium 34). This tests whether routeParam() hides taint from CodeQL.
# Setup:
#   CodeQL CLI 2.27.3, the version CI used.
#   Suites javascript-security-extended.qls + javascript-security-and-quality.qls, matching CI's
#   "security-extended,security-and-quality".
#   Clean git worktrees (no dist/, no node_modules). Not diff-informed.
#   Counted with the band script from security.yml's "Print CodeQL findings" step.
main 58d1a9b:     CodeQL results by security severity: {'high': 164, 'critical': 10, 'medium': 34, 'none': 1414}
PR head f8b7d50:  CodeQL results by security severity: {'high': 164, 'critical': 10, 'medium': 34, 'none': 1414}
(band, ruleId, file) multiset over critical+high+medium: 208 findings each side; 0 only in PR; 0 only in main.
# The local main numbers equal CI's main push run 40930898771 exactly, so the harness reproduces CI.

## Control: CI pull_request runs are diff-limited
# On pull_request events the CodeQL action runs queries with the PR's diff range:
#   database run-queries ... --additional-packs=.../pr-diff-range --extension-packs=codeql-action/pr-diff-range
#   (from PR #427's SAST log, job 124238432907)
# This narrows results to the diff. Push runs on main are full-scope.
PR #427 (lockfile-only vitest bump, no code change), CI job 124238432907:
  CodeQL results by security severity: {'high': 117, 'medium': 2, 'none': 1414}   (no critical)
  Its critical/high findings are a strict subset of main's: 0 only in #427; 57 only in main.
# Conclusion: the low CodeQL counts on #432's PR runs come from diff-informed analysis, not from
# routeParam(). On a full-scope run nothing is lost.

## Mechanism check: CodeQL follows taint through the helper
# Minimal repro: the same routeParam() source, fed into fetch(), pg.query() and res.send().
# js/request-forgery, js/sql-injection and js/reflected-xss each flag BOTH the raw req.params form
# and the routeParam(req.params.x) form. This still holds with 200 extra files and ~1,400 helper call sites.

## Decision
# No CodeQL model pack is added: CodeQL analyzes routeParam()'s body directly (founder decision 2026-11-01, option B).
